# L §8 What a result reads (tally 2.1.7 R1, issue #140; #127): a read of day d reads the walk's prefix through d, so a
# projection's walk that fails on day D (here the decision's tie, 2026-05-01) refuses only the reads that reach D,
# and answers an earlier day's read in either order: f_long_short's second term, bal(konto, 2026-03-31), is 800.00 as
# f_short alone is. 2.1.6's refcore refused every read after the failing one, so the line depended on its order.
=== m.tally
model p
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-15
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented probe for F5"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

index month = month 2026-01..2026-12

place konto: accounts DUK lives 2026-01-01..

input prio: int

input amt: money DUK

input dec_day: date

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

input pay: money DUK

input rent: money DUK

input off: int

move salary[m in month]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay

move rent_pay[m in month]: transfers
  on add_days(start_of(m), off)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount rent

move pick[k in month]: transfers
  on dec_day
  at dec_day
  reads konto
  ties by add_days(start_of(k), prio)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt + 0 * bal(konto, dec_day start)

ask f_long_short: low(konto, 2026-01-20 .. 2026-06-30) from 2026-01-20, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) from 2026-01-20

ask f_short_long: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) from 2026-01-20, low(konto, 2026-01-20 .. 2026-06-30) from 2026-01-20

version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 1000.00
  rent = 900.00
  off = 9
  opening[konto] = 500.00 at 2026-01-01 start
  amt = 5.00
  dec_day = 2026-05-01

version later
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-02-01
  prio = 1
=== expect f_long_short f_short_long
f_long_short: (refused: RUN-TIE pick: its ties by is a hole, 800.00 DUK)
...
f_short_long: (800.00 DUK, refused: RUN-TIE pick: its ties by is a hole)
...
